   "speech": "Among people possessed of the keenest spiritual sensitivity, Gratien Duplay occupied that restless place where the force of life’s excitements comes close to breaking through into madness. Very frequent among his critical states were those moments when, freely yielding to the impressions that came flooding in upon him, he would suddenly shudder in an alluringly terrible presentiment of an instantaneous illumination, whose meaning would be the revelation of the meaning of everything. Naturally, human reason, with an instinctive convulsion, thrust back such a deluge, and the outburst of nerves gave way to exhaustion; otherwise something vaster than consciousness, founded perhaps upon a Homeric synthesis, must inevitably have shattered the mind, like a village mill set to work by Niagara.",
